# .doctrine/agent_identities — who counts as an AGENT in a commit-message attribution trailer
# (COMMIT-MESSAGE). Read as of the last commit. One entry per line:
#   address <ERE>   matched, case-insensitively, against the e-mail in `Name <e-mail>`
#   name <ERE>      matched, case-insensitively, against the WHOLE name (anchored)
# Nothing is built into the check: every agent identity is data here (NT-09). A HUMAN named Claude,
# Gemini or Cursor is never an agent: match products exactly, or a product followed by a model
# family and a version; match agents' mail addresses, never a human's.
# `line <ERE>`: a BODY line some harnesses add as attribution (matched case-insensitively against each line)
line ^(🤖 )?generated with (\[|[A-Za-z])
line ^claude-session:
address noreply@anthropic\.com$
address noreply@openai\.com$
address noreply@google\.com$
address copilot@users\.noreply\.github\.com$
name ^(Claude( Code)?|Claude (Opus|Sonnet|Haiku|Fable|Mythos)( [0-9][0-9.]*)?|Codex|ChatGPT|GitHub Copilot|Copilot|Gemini( CLI)?|Cursor|Aider|Windsurf|Devin|Amp)$
